1
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,190
Is anyone up here?

2
00:00:24,323 --> 00:00:27,393
Careful, the third step is broken.

3
00:00:28,921 --> 00:00:32,541
Tom? I thought you left on the morning boat.

4
00:00:35,820 --> 00:00:39,385
The boat never came. The sea was too rough.

5
00:00:40,638 --> 00:00:43,818
So you climbed a lighthouse to wait?

6
00:00:46,694 --> 00:00:50,259
I came to fix the radio. Nobody else would.

7
00:00:52,539 --> 00:00:55,829
That radio hasn't worked in ten years.

8
00:00:57,032 --> 00:01:00,707
Eleven. My father was the last one to use it.

9
00:01:03,483 --> 00:01:06,058
I'm sorry. I didn't know.

10
00:01:07,189 --> 00:01:10,644
Hand me the small screwdriver, would you?

11
00:01:13,162 --> 00:01:14,857
This one?

12
00:01:16,101 --> 00:01:19,061
No, the one with the red handle.

13
00:01:20,379 --> 00:01:23,449
Why does it matter so much to you?

14
00:01:25,935 --> 00:01:30,050
Because the island has no other way to call for help.

15
00:01:30,650 --> 00:01:31,850
[wind howling]

16
00:01:33,943 --> 00:01:37,948
The phone line went down with the storm last night.

17
00:01:41,156 --> 00:01:43,896
And Mrs. Hale is still sick.

18
00:01:46,936 --> 00:01:50,501
The doctor is on the mainland until Friday.

19
00:01:51,718 --> 00:01:54,678
Then let's make this thing talk.

20
00:01:57,727 --> 00:02:01,017
Do you know anything about old radios?

21
00:02:02,191 --> 00:02:06,416
My grandmother built one from a kit when I was a child.

22
00:02:08,189 --> 00:02:10,049
Did it work?

23
00:02:12,998 --> 00:02:16,288
It caught a station from Norway, once.

24
00:02:17,754 --> 00:02:19,504
Only once?

25
00:02:21,971 --> 00:02:25,976
She said once was enough to prove it could be done.

26
00:02:28,868 --> 00:02:32,378
Look at this wire. It's completely burned.

27
00:02:35,376 --> 00:02:37,676
Lightning, probably.

28
00:02:40,637 --> 00:02:44,147
Is there any copper wire in the storeroom?

29
00:02:47,534 --> 00:02:50,769
There's a whole box under the stairs.

30
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:55,200
I'll get it. Don't touch anything.

31
00:02:58,199 --> 00:03:00,554
I wasn't planning to.

32
00:03:02,212 --> 00:03:04,567
Here. Is this enough?

33
00:03:05,908 --> 00:03:09,253
More than enough. Hold the lamp closer.

34
00:03:12,745 --> 00:03:15,210
Your hands are shaking.

35
00:03:18,186 --> 00:03:21,696
It's the cold. This room was never heated.

36
00:03:24,862 --> 00:03:26,832
Take my scarf.

37
00:03:29,569 --> 00:03:31,319
Thank you.

38
00:03:34,181 --> 00:03:37,691
Now we need power. The batteries are dead.

39
00:03:41,411 --> 00:03:44,591
What about the generator downstairs?

40
00:03:48,823 --> 00:03:52,663
It needs fuel, and the fuel is in the boathouse.

41
00:03:54,532 --> 00:03:58,042
In this wind? You'd be blown into the sea.

42
00:03:59,672 --> 00:04:02,742
Then we wait for the wind to drop.

43
00:04:03,342 --> 00:04:04,542
[waves crashing]

44
00:04:06,471 --> 00:04:09,376
Mrs. Hale can't wait that long.

45
00:04:12,214 --> 00:04:14,844
Is there a rope somewhere?

46
00:04:18,907 --> 00:04:21,702
On the hook by the door. Why?

47
00:04:23,710 --> 00:04:26,780
Tie it around my waist. I'm going.

48
00:04:27,380 --> 00:04:28,580
[door creaks]

49
00:04:31,210 --> 00:04:33,015
You're mad.

50
00:04:34,593 --> 00:04:37,113
Probably. Hold on tight.

51
00:04:45,310 --> 00:04:47,720
Mara! Can you hear me?

52
00:04:51,987 --> 00:04:55,442
I'm at the boathouse! The door is jammed!

53
00:04:56,042 --> 00:04:57,242
[radio static]

54
00:04:59,809 --> 00:05:02,384
Kick it! Near the bottom!

55
00:05:05,389 --> 00:05:08,239
It's open! I can see the cans!

56
00:05:12,303 --> 00:05:14,493
How many are full?

57
00:05:17,927 --> 00:05:20,062
Two! Maybe three!

58
00:05:23,142 --> 00:05:25,772
Take two. Don't be greedy.

59
00:05:28,802 --> 00:05:31,102
Pull me back slowly!

60
00:05:33,699 --> 00:05:36,329
I've got you. Keep coming.

61
00:05:40,268 --> 00:05:42,513
I'm here. I'm here.

62
00:05:45,173 --> 00:05:47,803
You're soaked to the bone.

63
00:05:51,127 --> 00:05:53,262
But we have fuel.

64
00:06:00,475 --> 00:06:03,710
Pour it in. Slowly, or it will flood.

65
00:06:07,165 --> 00:06:09,355
Now pull the cord.

66
00:06:12,620 --> 00:06:14,260
Nothing.

67
00:06:18,736 --> 00:06:21,256
Again. Harder this time.

68
00:06:23,252 --> 00:06:25,167
It's running!

69
00:06:27,517 --> 00:06:30,202
The lights are on upstairs!

70
00:06:33,542 --> 00:06:36,062
Quick, before it stalls.

71
00:06:37,141 --> 00:06:40,486
Switch it on. The big dial on the left.

72
00:06:43,102 --> 00:06:44,962
Only static.

73
00:06:46,550 --> 00:06:50,390
Turn it slowly. The coast guard is near the end.

74
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:54,320
Wait. Did you hear that?

75
00:06:55,527 --> 00:06:58,157
A voice. Go back a little.

76
00:06:58,757 --> 00:06:59,957
[wind howling]

77
00:07:01,845 --> 00:07:05,795
This is the coast guard. Please identify yourself.

78
00:07:08,188 --> 00:07:12,083
This is Gull Island lighthouse. We need a doctor.

79
00:07:16,292 --> 00:07:20,297
An old woman is sick, and the phone lines are down.

80
00:07:21,879 --> 00:07:25,279
Understood, Gull Island. How bad is she?

81
00:07:27,685 --> 00:07:31,305
High fever since yesterday. She can't stand.

82
00:07:33,277 --> 00:07:36,952
We'll send a boat as soon as the wind allows.

83
00:07:38,432 --> 00:07:41,887
Probably at dawn. Keep this channel open.

84
00:07:44,393 --> 00:07:46,638
We will. Thank you.

85
00:07:49,564 --> 00:07:52,634
Your father would have been proud.

86
00:07:56,107 --> 00:07:59,232
He would have said I took too long.

87
00:08:03,684 --> 00:08:06,424
Eleven years is a long time.

88
00:08:08,756 --> 00:08:12,321
Not for the radio. For coming back up here.

89
00:08:14,128 --> 00:08:16,538
Why did you stay away?

90
00:08:17,829 --> 00:08:21,614
Every step of this staircase reminds me of him.

91
00:08:23,143 --> 00:08:25,443
Even the broken one?

92
00:08:28,748 --> 00:08:32,423
Especially the broken one. He never fixed it.

93
00:08:33,465 --> 00:08:36,590
Maybe we should leave it like that.

94
00:08:37,190 --> 00:08:38,390
[waves crashing]

95
00:08:40,499 --> 00:08:42,579
Maybe we should.

96
00:08:43,594 --> 00:08:46,884
Look. The sky is clearing in the west.

97
00:08:49,350 --> 00:08:51,595
The boat will come.

98
00:08:53,887 --> 00:08:56,572
I'll go and tell Mrs. Hale.

99
00:08:59,554 --> 00:09:02,734
Take the lamp. The path is slippery.

100
00:09:07,070 --> 00:09:08,710
And you?

101
00:09:11,514 --> 00:09:14,529
Someone has to stay by the radio.

102
00:09:17,691 --> 00:09:20,541
Then I'll bring you some soup.

103
00:09:23,908 --> 00:09:25,383
Mara?

104
00:09:26,572 --> 00:09:27,992
Yes?

105
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:34,550
Thank you for staying.

